    {
      "name": "GPIO13",
      "label": "GPIO13 (Button)",
      "codeName": "13",
      "capabilities": [
        "digital_input",
        "digital_output",
        "pwm_output",
        "button"
      ],
      "notes": "BOOT button — onboard bootloader-select pushbutton, also usable as a general input when application code is running. Not aliased in this board's pins_arduino.h (no PIN_BUTTON define shipped by arduino-pico for this board) — added directly as a chipGpios entry; raw pin number 13 is still usable via pinMode()/digitalRead() on arduino-pico. Active-low with the RP2040's internal pull-up enabled (no external pull-up on this line). Confirmed via Zephyr's adafruit_itsybitsy_rp2040.dts gpio_keys node (gpios = <&gpio0 13 (GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW | GPIO_PULL_UP)>), Adafruit's own pinouts guide (\"This button is also usable as an input in CircuitPython code, on pin board.BUTTON. It is on RP2040 pin GPIO13\"), and CircuitPython's own pins.c for this board.\nCheck if available on board"
    },
